Fruit Ninja for webOS (HP TouchPad) — an apkenv port
====================================================

This is the Android build of Halfbrick's **Fruit Ninja** (1.8.8, the free
edition) running *natively* on webOS. There is no ACL (OpenMobile's full
Android runtime) and no Dalvik: apkenv is a slim shim — a gingerbread bionic
linker loaded as a library, a fake-JNI layer, a webOS SDL/PDL backend, and a
per-game module that plays the part of the game's Android Java host.

Fruit Ninja's engine is Halfbrick **Mortar** (lib/armeabi/libmortargame.so). It
renders through its own GLES2 device and mixes its own audio; the module
(apkenv/modules/mortar.c) answers the Java contract around it — file manager,
device properties, preferences, the KeyStore save file, dialogs, and the
AudioTrack sink the engine pushes its mix into.

WHAT WORKS
----------
  Full-screen landscape 1024x768, the game's own ES2 renderer.
  Menus, mode select, Classic / Arcade / Zen, slicing, scoring, bombs.
  Sound and music (44100 Hz stereo, the engine's own mixer).
  Saves and settings persist across restarts and reinstalls.

WHAT IS MISSING, AND WHY
------------------------
  Anything that needs a network or a Google account: ads, in-app purchase,
  leaderboards, the YouTube trailer on the first-run screen, push
  notifications. The shim reports the device as offline, which is a state the
  game already handles — it shows its own "no connection" screens. The engine
  still retries its ad-media downloads in the background; they fail harmlessly.

  Multiplayer (it is same-device "VS", and untested here).

LAYOUT OF THIS APP DIRECTORY
----------------------------
  apkenv            The host binary (native ARM ELF). On launch it self-locates
                    (/proc/self/exe), cd's here, picks the game under android/,
                    and runs it.
  appinfo.json      webOS app manifest (type:pdk, main:apkenv).
  icon.png          Launcher icon.
  README            This file.

  libs/webos/       webOS-side host libraries, loaded by apkenv's OWN userspace
                    linker: harvested Android 2.3 (gingerbread) bionic
                    libc/libm/libstdc++/liblog/libz — the runtime the game's
                    native code was built against — plus the TouchPad's own
                    libEGL.so.

  android/          The Android bits. fruitninja.apk is shipped whole: apkenv
                    reads the engine's native .so and all 87 MB of game assets
                    straight out of it at runtime, through the engine's own zip
                    reader. apkenv.env holds launch settings (see below).

RUNTIME-WRITABLE DATA (the app directory is read-only at runtime)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  /media/internal/.apkenv/fruitninja.apk/   saves (KeyStore.dat), preferences,
                                            cache, and the apk's extracted
                                            native libs.
  /media/internal/apkenv-com.apkenv.fruitninja.log
                                            this app's stdout/stderr — a jailed
                                            PDK app's stdio goes nowhere else.
                                            Rewritten on every launch.

LAUNCH SETTINGS (android/apkenv.env)
------------------------------------
  APKENV_MORTAR_DIALOG_BUTTON=0   How to answer a dialog the shim cannot draw.
                                  0 = the negative button, 1 = positive,
                                  -1 = leave it unanswered. 0 is correct here:
                                  the dialog this build raises is the quit
                                  confirmation, and 1 would quit the game.

SOURCE AND NOTES
----------------
  Module:  apkenv/modules/mortar.c
  Trail:   plan/FRUITNINJA.md  (what broke, and what the fixes were)
  Contract: plan/fruitninja-contract.txt  (the engine->Java surface)
  Method:  PORTING-PLAYBOOK.md, android-port-shim.md
